     "replacement": "If $a\\times b=0$\n\nThen $a=0$ or $b=0$ (or both).\n\nThis holds for any numbers or expressions $a$ and $b$.\n\nFor example, if $(x+a)(x+b)=0$\n\nThen $x+a=0$\n\nor $x+b=0$",
